      "description": "Watch Orlando City SC vs Nashville SC highlights and goals from Major League Soccer on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 26, 2026. Orlando City SC and Nashville SC faced off in a tightly contested MLS encounter that tested the tactical resolve of both sides. Fans gathered on July 26, 2026, to witness a match defined by defensive organization and a decisive spark from the bench. A Strategic Standoff in the First Half The match began with both teams prioritizing stability, leading to a cagey opening period. Orlando City SC attempted to dictate the tempo, but Nashville SC remained disciplined in their defensive shape. The physical nature of the contest was highlighted in the 20th minute when Tiago Carvalho was shown a yellow card for a robust challenge. As the half progressed, chances remained scarce, and both managers headed into the break knowing that a tactical adjustment would be required to break the deadlock. The Impact of Tyrese Spicer The second half saw the introduction of fresh energy that eventually tilted the scales. In the 53rd minute, Tyrese Spicer replaced Tiago Carvalho , a substitution that proved to be the turning point of the afternoon. Spicer immediately stretched the Nashville SC defense with his movement, creating more space for his teammates in the final third. In the 72nd minute, the breakthrough finally arrived. Justin Ellis played a pivotal role, delivering a perfectly weighted assist to find Tyrese Spicer . With clinical precision, Spicer found the back of the net, sending the home crowd into raptures. The goal forced Nashville SC to push forward, leading to a series of tactical substitutions, including the introduction of Daniel Lovitz and Edvard Tagseth in an attempt to salvage a point. Closing Stages and the Final Whistle As the clock ticked down, the game became a battle of nerves. Orlando City SC managed the closing stages professionally, utilizing substitutions like Wilder Cartagena and Harvey Sarajian to shore up the midfield. Nashville SC made a final throw of the dice by bringing on Woobens Pacius during the eight minutes of stoppage time, but the home side’s defense held firm. When the referee blew the final whistle at 90+8 minutes, it confirmed a hard-fought victory for the hosts, orchestrated by a game-changing performance from their substitutes."
