      "description": "Watch Nashville SC vs CF Montreal highlights and goals from Major League Soccer on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 23, 2026. Major League Soccer delivered a tightly contested battle on July 23, 2026 , as Nashville SC welcomed CF Montreal for a mid-season clash. The match was a display of tactical discipline, with both sides searching for a breakthrough in a game of fine margins. A Cagey Opening Period From the start, both teams looked organized, prioritizing defensive solidity over reckless attacking. Nashville SC attempted to control possession, but CF Montreal 's compact shape made it difficult to create clear-cut opportunities. The first half progressed with high energy but few strikes on target, leading to a goalless stalemate at the interval as both managers headed to the locker rooms to adjust their strategies. Surridge Steps Up from the Spot The intensity shifted in the second half as the game opened up. Following a series of substitutions, including Andy Najar replacing Josh Bauer for the hosts, the pressure finally told in the 68th minute. The referee awarded a penalty to Nashville, and Sam Surridge stepped up to the spot. With composure and precision, Surridge fired the ball home to give Nashville SC a 1-0 lead, a goal that would prove to be the defining moment of the contest. Late Drama and Defensive Resilience As the clock ticked toward full-time, the atmosphere grew increasingly tense. CF Montreal made several late changes, bringing on Jack Maher and Charles-Emile Brunet in a bid to rescue a point. The closing stages were physical, resulting in yellow cards for goal-scorer Sam Surridge and Montreal's Prince Osei Owusu . Despite nearly eight minutes of added time and relentless pressure from the visitors, Nashville's backline held firm until the final whistle blew at 90+8', securing all three points for the home side."
